<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Sideload only, and the split is deliberate.

    A drive in a container is a symlink in `dosdevices`, and Wine reads through
    it with this app's own uid — so reaching the phone's storage from the guest
    needs the app to be allowed to read the phone's storage. That is
    MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE: a settings toggle rather than a dialog, and a
    Play-policy sensitive permission that this project has no grounds to claim
    in a store build.

    The `play` flavour therefore does not declare it and cannot map a folder.
    The alternative there is SAF, which hands back a `content://` tree — not a
    path, so there is nothing to symlink and Wine cannot open it. Better to
    refuse in words than to ship a picker that half works. See
    docs/DRIVE-MAPPING.md.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE" />
</manifest>
